needs at least 3 moves to reach d2: g2-f3-e4-d3 or similar, but we can protect). Black can also use rook or knight to support. This creates a passed pawn that will likely become a queen, leading to overwhelming material advantage and checkmate. Other moves like knight checks or rook moves are less forcing and allow white counterplay.\n\nThus, I choose P: d3-d2.\n\nAnswer: P: d3-d2"}
