ralizing the king is often the top priority. **K: f7-e6** brings the king toward the center where it can participate in the game, potentially support pawn advances, and restrict the opponent’s king and knight. Additionally, with the white knight on h7, it is somewhat trapped; centralizing the king prepares to march and attack it. The knight move a7-c6 is also good, but king activity is more crucial in such an open endgame.\n\nAnswer: K: f7-e6'}
