ndeed only safe square from g7 after Qf7+ is h6. That forces Kh6. Then we can play Qf7-g6#. Checkmate in 2 moves.\n\nReason: This forces checkmate quickly. Other queen checks don’t lead to immediate forced mate sequence as cleanly (maybe some do but longer). Qf5-f7+ is the most forcing move. King moves to help are unnecessary because queen alone can deliver mate with proper coordination. So Qf5-f7+ then next move Qg6#.\n\nThus final choice: Q: f5-f7.\n\nAnswer: Q: f5-f7"}
